    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36349" root="قوب" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَائِبَةٌ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَاوِبَةٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُوبٌ</span>; the former in eight
places, and the latter in one place. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَائِبَةُ قُوبٍ</span>
means <i>An empty egg:</i> to such, in a trad., Mekkeh
is likened when devoid of pilgrims. (O.)

